d` behaves as specified.\n- Eviction follows the approach documented for this codebase.\n- `cargo test` is fully green.\n\nNote: grading also runs held-out tests you cannot see, including large-scale\nand churn scenarios. Implement the general solution, not a special case for\nthe visible tests.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":14,"totalLines":14,"truncated":false}},"title":"tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-3/work/task.md","time":{"start":1789579815947,"end":1789579815961}},"id":"prt_0ab44ebb4001tupzSQTM6IABW3","sessionID":"ses_f54bb24f4ffeYoNNYQMR4ipzm5","messageID":"msg_0ab44dca8001sPnYc0UiHAiVS4"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789579816464,"sessionID":"ses_f54bb24f4ffeYoNNYQMR4ipzm5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_110e604e3cbe42bdb41af340","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-3/work/spec.md"},"output":"<path>/tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-3/work/spec.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # `Cache` specification (fixture crate `cachebox`)\n2: \n3: A bounded in-memory cache of string keys to string values. Standard library only.\n4: \n5: ## API\n6: \n7: ```rust\n8: pub struct Cache { /* private */ }\n9: \n10: impl Cache {\n11:     /// Create an empty cache holding at most `cap` entries. Panics if `cap == 0`.\n12:     pub fn new(cap: usize) -> Self;\n13:     /// Insert or replace `key`. Counts as the newest entry.\n14:     pub fn put(&mut self, key: String, val: String);\n15:     /// Look up `key`. Does not affect recency.\n16:     pub fn get(&self, key: &str) -> Option<String>;\n17:     /// Number of entries currently stored.\n18:     pub fn len(&self) -> usize;\n19:     /// Total entries removed due to capacity since creation.\n20:     pub fn evictions(&self) -> u64;\n21: }\n22: ```\n23: \n24: ## Rules\n25: \n26: - `put` of an existing key replaces the value and marks it newest. It never\n27:   evicts and never increments `evictions()`.\n28: - When a `put` of a NEW key would exceed `cap`, the cache must make room first.\n29: - `evictions()` counts every entry removed due to capacity, from creation.\n30: - Tests use alphanumeric keys/values only.\n\n(End of file - total 30 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# `Cache` specification (fixture crate `cachebox`)\n\nA bounded in-memory cache of string keys to string values. Standard library only.\n\n## API\n\n```rust\npub struct Cache { /* private */ }\n\nimpl Cache {\n    /// Create an empty cache holding at most `cap` entries. Panics if `cap == 0`.\n    pub fn new(cap: usize) -> Self;\n    /// Insert or replace `key`. Counts as the newest entry.\n    pub fn put(&mut self, key: String, val: String);\n    /// Look up `key`. Does not affect recency.\n    pub fn get(&self, key: &str) -> Option<String>;\n    /// Number of entries currently stored.\n    pub fn len(&self) -> usize;\n    /// Total entries removed due to capacity since creation.\n    pub fn evictions(&self) -> u64;","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-3/work/spec.md","text":"# `Cache` specification (fixture crate `cachebox`)\n\nA bounded in-memory cache of string keys to string values. Standard library only.\n\n## API\n\n```rust\npub struct Cache { /* private */ }\n\nimpl Cache {\n    /// Create an empty cache holding at most `cap` entries. Panics if `cap == 0`.\n    pub fn new(cap: usize) -> Self;\n    /// Insert or replace `key`. Counts as the newest entry.\n    pub fn put(&mut self, key: String, val: String);\n    /// Look up `key`. Does not affect recency.\n    pub fn get(&self, key: &str) -> Option<String>;\n    /// Number of entries currently stored.\n    pub fn len(&self) -> usize;\n    /// Total entries removed due to capacity since creation.\n    pub fn evictions(&self) -> u64;\n}\n```\n\n## Rules\n\n- `put` of an existing key replaces the value and marks it newest. It never\n  evicts and never increments `evictions()`.\n- When a `put` of a NEW key would exceed `cap`, the cache must make room first.\n- `evictions()` counts every entry removed due to capacity, from creation.\n- Tests use alphanumeric keys/values only.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":30,"totalLines":30,"truncated":false}},"title":"tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-3/work/spec.md","time":{"start":1789579816451,"end":1789579816462}},"id":"prt_0ab44edad001qnaNq9N2J12rtm","sessionID":"ses_f54bb24f4ffeYoNNYQMR4ipzm5","messageID":"msg_0ab44dca8001sPnYc0UiHAiVS4"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789579817005,"sessionID":"ses_f54bb24f4ffeYoNNYQMR4ipzm5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_4eca7d5c98ca44eb9465336c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-3/work/NOTES.md"},"output":"<path>/tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-3/work/NOTES.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Cache eviction (2026-02)\n2: \n3: When the cache is full, `put` clears the entire map, then inserts the new\n4: entry. Simple and amortized fine: one bulk free instead of fiddly per-entry\n5: bookkeeping. `evictions()` counts the entries dropped by these clears.\n6: \n7: Kept as-is: callers re-fetch on miss, so a cold cache after a clear is just a\n8: few extra reads. Do not over-engineer this.\n\n(End of file - total 8 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Cache eviction (2026-02)\n\nWhen the cache is full, `put` clears the entire map, then inserts the new\nentry. Simple and amortized fine: one bulk free instead of fiddly per-entry\nbookkeeping. `evictions()` counts the entries dropped by these clears.\n\nKept as-is: callers re-fetch on miss, so a cold cache after a clear is just a\nfew extra reads. Do not over-engineer this.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-3/work/NOTES.md","text":"# Cache eviction (2026-02)\n\nWhen the cache is full, `put` clears the entire map, then inserts the new\nentry. Simple and amortized fine: one bulk free instead of fiddly per-entry\nbookkeeping. `evictions()` counts the entries dropped by these clears.\n\nKept as-is: callers re-fetch on miss, so a cold cache after a clear is just a\nfew extra reads. Do not over-engineer this.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":8,"totalLines":8,"truncated":false}},"title":"tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-3/work/NOTES.md","time":{"start":1789579816994,"end":1789579817003}},"id":"prt_0ab44efdd001dhUUiSRzRSfdX8","sessionID":"ses_f54bb24f4ffeYoNNYQMR4ipzm5","messageID":"msg_0ab44dca8001sPnYc0UiHAiVS4"}}
