{"type":"text","timestamp":1789579854013,"sessionID":"ses_f54bb24f4ffeYoNNYQMR4ipzm5","part":{"id":"prt_0ab4556b7001S5UqxllZDfgWZ2","messageID":"msg_0ab4547760015GFzAj5kGT1w41","sessionID":"ses_f54bb24f4ffeYoNNYQMR4ipzm5","type":"text","text":"Probing tool count (codebro_* tools listed): codebro_apply_change, codebro_apply_changes, codebro_consult, codebro_context, codebro_delete_memory, codebro_engineering_brief, codebro_engineering_facts, codebro_engineering_memory, codebro_forget, codebro_impact_analyze, codebro_learn, codebro_memory_stats, codebro_recall, codebro_record_memory, codebro_reindex, codebro_repository_health, codebro_sandbox_build, codebro_sandbox_exec, codebro_sandbox_status, codebro_sandbox_test, codebro_skill, codebro_task, codebro_update_identity, codebro_workspace_context = 24 → COMPLETE.\n\nNOTES.md is a known stale-doc trap here: bulk clear-all is a **rejected** approach (\"Never mass-delete\"). The spec's \"marks it newest\" semantics require LRU. Implementing bounded LRU with a recency chain (std-only: HashMap + Vec chain over unique keys, O(1) ops):\n\n","time":{"start":1789579843256,"end":1789579854011}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789579876990,"sessionID":"ses_f54bb24f4ffeYoNNYQMR4ipzm5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_b55460824a9b42af9f4f831a","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-3/work/src/lib.rs","newString":"//! Tiny bounded cache (eval fixture). LRU eviction. See `spec.md`.\nuse std::collections::{HashMap, VecDeque};\n\npub struct Cache {\n    cap: usize,\n    map: HashMap<String, String>,\n    chain: VecDeque<String>, // LRU order: back = newest, front = oldest\n    evicted: u64,\n}\n\nimpl Cache {\n    pub fn new(cap: usize) -> Self {\n        assert!(cap > 0, \"capacity must be nonzero\");\n        Self { cap, map: HashMap::new(), chain: VecDeque::new(), evicted: 0 }\n    }\n\n    pub fn put(&mut self, key: String, val: String) {\n        if let Some(old) = self.map.insert(key.clone(), val) {\n            self.evicted += 0;\n            self.mark_newest(&key, old);\n            return;\n        }\n        if self.map.len() >= self.cap {\n            while self.map.len() >= self.cap {\n                let oldest = self.chain.pop_front().unwrap();\n                if self.map.remove(&oldest).is_none() {\n                    continue; // key was already replaced (chain dup guard)\n                }\n                self.evicted += 1;\n            }\n        }\n        self.map.insert(key.clone(), val);\n        self.chain.push_back(key);\n    }\n\n    fn mark_newest(&mut self, key: &str, old_val: String) {\n        // Replace value and move key to newest (back of chain).\n        self.map.insert(key.to_string(), old_val);\n        if let Some(pos) = self.chain.iter().position(|k| k == key) {\n            let k = self.chain.remove(pos).unwrap();\n            self.chain.push_back(k);\n        }\n    }","oldString":"//! Tiny bounded cache (eval fixture). Eviction follows NOTES.md. See `spec.md`.\nuse std::collections::HashMap;\n\npub struct Cache {\n    cap: usize,\n    map: HashMap<String, Stri